{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Peter's Dating Misadventures", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "I Give Up!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Expressing an Opinion About Past Events (Simple Past vs Past Perfect)", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Perfect tense to identify and talk about an 'earlier past'. <br /> You use the Simple Past to talk about a finished action that happened at a specific time in the past. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you are talking about a past event, you can refer to something that happened at an earlier time to that past event by using the <span class=\"underline\">Past Perfect</span> tense.<br /><br />  The structure of the Past Perfect is:<br /><br />  Subject + had + past participle<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">He started dating again after he <span class=\"strong\">had met </span>his old flame by chance.</span><br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">first</span>? He met his old flame.<br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">later</span>? He started dating again.<br /><br />  You use the Past Perfect tense (not Simple Past) when you want to talk about how long something had continued <span class=\"strong\">up to a past moment</span>. <br /> Example:<br />  <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">had thought </span>that relationships were hard work until I met several couples for some of my interviews. </span><br /> You use the Simple Past tense to talk about the action that happened after that prior action in the Past Perfect tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I hadn't realized how much I cared for you guys until I left for my trip around the world last year.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When I saw you guys at the airport, it felt as if I had never left.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Expressing Understanding Using Modals ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty.<br /> You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to describe degrees of certainty. You can use modals with the Present Perfect to talk about the possibility of a past event that is not clear in the present context. Example: <span class=\"italic\">You<span class=\"strong\"> must have missed</span> us a lot! </span>  Must = it's very likely  Must not / Could not / Can't = it's not possible May / Might / Can / Could = it's possible May not / Might not = it's possible this is not true", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Modal </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Meaning </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  It must happen more often than you think. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's very likely that it happens more often than you think.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">   You may be right.  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible that you are right.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> So you mean it might not be hopeless? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's not likely that it is hopeless.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "old flame", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to refer to an ex-girlfriend", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He started dating again after he had met his old flame by chance at the gym.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words to review.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to move on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to concentrate one's attention or emotions on other matters in recovering from a setback or difficulty", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: After a year I was ready to move on.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to relieve ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to free from pain, anxiety, or distress", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It relieves a lot of the stress I've had lately.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "better late than never", "type": "name"}, {"content": " used when it's better for something to happen late than not at all", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Better late than never. You couldn't possibly regret it!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "incomprehensible", "type": "name"}, {"content": "impossible to understand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I just think that love is incomprehensible to me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "hopeless", "type": "name"}, {"content": "desperate and with no hope ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It might look hopeless now, but there must be something you can do!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Think about the last time you had a bad experience at a restaurant.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write detailed notes about the event (e.g. Where did you go? What did you order?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compile your notes into a complete paragraph about the event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the paragraph with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I make notes about a past event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a paragraph about a past event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my experiences with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn8le08ob11re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn8le08ob11re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tThanks for the drinks, Sally. It's good to go out with a friend who understands you, sometimes. It relieves a lot of the stress I've had lately.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:\t\tI know the feeling, Peter. I hadn't realized how much I cared for you guys until I left for my trip around the world last year.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tYou must have missed us a lot!\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:\t\tI certainly did. I met all sorts of interesting people, but after a year I was ready to move on. When I saw you guys at the airport, it felt as if I had never left."}, {"image": "engenn8le08ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "26100", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tI wish I could have felt the same way about any of my dates! My friend Matt told me about how he started dating again after he had met his old flame by chance at the gym. They're so happy together now.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:\t\tBetter late than never, I suppose. It must happen more often than you think.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tYou may be right. I just think that love is incomprehensible to me.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:\t\tIt could feel that way sometimes, but I assure you that it can be quite simple as well. I had thought that relationships were hard work until I met several couples for some of my interviews. They showed me how it's possible to love someone your whole life and be happy about it."}, {"image": "engenn8le08ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "60500", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tSo you mean it might not be hopeless?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:\t\tThat's exactly what I mean!\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tWell, I don't know. I give up!"}], "audiosrc": "engenn8le08ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le08ob11re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "text", "contents": [{"value": "Look, Gabriel, stop living in the past. You need to comprehend that love is something you take seriously, but it's bigger than just one relationship. An old flame might always be there and it doesn't mean you must wait for this person your entire life. Learn to move on! You must have felt hopeless after breaking up with her, but that's not a reason to stay alone forever. You must start at some point, better late than never!", "type": "p"}], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about socializing, feelings and reactions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about life experiences or explain my opinion about past events.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can show I understand someone's feelings or situation.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you think it's possible to be in love with someone your entire life? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " If you could go back in time and change one event in your life, what would it be?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let's review!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " \nPeter is <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">at his wit's end</span>. What can Sally say to make it better?\n", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Somet